A||||4||Fiero64||Head Gasket Problem||||8
Z||000000||Fiero64||10-02-1999||11:02 AM||||I just bought a 1984 Fiero for virtuually nothing but it needs a head gasket and cooling fan.  The car is about 750 miles away and I have no way of towing so I figure I'll repair it where it is and drive it back to Texas.  Any ideas on what "further problems" I can possibly expect to run into with the 2.5 engine?  We don't think that the car was heated too severely......Thanks for the help.....Wayne||||reg||8
Z||000001||batboy||10-02-1999||12:00 PM||||If the cooling fan don't work and it got so hot that the head gasket blew, then there is always the possibility of a cracked head too. I think I'd tow it back, U-Haul has flat bed trailers for rent.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-02-1999||09:11 PM||||definatly visit U-haul or Ryder. Unless you have time to spend a couple days there..... or have a spare head. If the thing quit from an ovreheat it's very likely warped or cracked.<P>If it got that hot the reality is that the motor may need a rebuild. You often cook the rings out in those conditions. Even after you fix just the head odds are it's not going to hold up to much longer. <P>Carefully check compression if you do just the head. Carefully check the block deck for warping as well.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Linx||10-03-1999||12:08 AM||||Man- I cant imagine doing that kind of work in the driveway, and over a weekend.  You'd have to carry a load of tools and parts, or know where to find them and count on them being there.<P>I, too, rebuilt my Fiero; purchased cheap and dead in the driveway.  It had been ruined in much the same way.  The block rebuild was what I expected and went easily.  What I didnt expect was everything else going bad, or bad already.  Days later, a waterpump.  Then emissions problems.  Alternator.  Oil leaks- lots of them.<P>Find a way to tow, or count on a chase vehicle.  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero64||10-03-1999||10:32 AM||||Fortunately, tools are NOT an issue...I'm a mechanic.  I was just basically wondering if there were any uncommon problems specific to the 2.5 that I needed to know about that may rear their ugly head after an overheating situation.  I DO know a couple things about the car, I bought it from my father who owns a small buy here/pay here car lot (he'd repo'd the Fiero).  As far as we know the car is in very good shape other than the head gasket and cooling fan situation....Thanks to you guys for all the help.............Wayne ||||reg||10
